      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Id like to add on to point 3\nspecifically for people with limited internet or slow internet\n\nA area in the setting that you can add your preferred max world size. and if a portal is dropped it will have a red version of the community labs banner around it warning that it exceeds this limit if that be the case. Player can still enter it its simply a strong visualization so they know that this is larger than they prefer.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-01T08:33:10.751Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The introduction to world size (how big a world is in MB) is nice, however it would be better if it was displayed in more areas as follows\n\n\n1. Invited to a world:\nUser1 invited you to The Hub (20MB).\n\n\n2. Social Menu when selecting people\nUser1 is in avatar world(200mb). Friends+\n\n\n3.Portals - Just anywhere visible\n\n\nThe process of having to cancel whatever menu, go to the world tab and search for the world name to see how large the world is isn't very practical. It should help the people with slower download speeds to consider if they want want to go before accepting the invite.",
